res\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d91f48c4ac9ef23cc3d2498625dc688326007249deaebc3f906aaaf8e66f1fff","event_uuid":"178fb9b9-0981-4008-9fad-527d4d45274a","position":{"commit_sha":"0bc9d2c87e8856af7b771f3cc6e9c1638577172e","position":"1786653954593956001-178fb9b9-0981-4008-9fad-527d4d45274a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f1db986edd655eb8a13146a25cf2161f266cfbf04b8d72355b2fecbac3c55cde","event_uuid":"80c8756e-5315-41ab-97e8-ec74af980184","position":{"commit_sha":"0bc9d2c87e8856af7b771f3cc6e9c1638577172e","position":"1786653955710037001-80c8756e-5315-41ab-97e8-ec74af980184"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f9688a8de6f868f9eecab1d1c1c4c66cd19be7a839e462735ca90a34a210276d","event_uuid":"d98cd0c7-b4cb-4330-af29-e22be9437654","position":{"commit_sha":"55103ee6dcefdeed3ac61e39ab39fee8319c37bd","position":"1786655301468664015-d98cd0c7-b4cb-4330-af29-e22be9437654"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786160107365143001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d98cd0c7-b4cb-4330-af29-e22be9437654","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"574a-3152-5cef-430e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOnce a store actually syncs more than one tracker project, an older rebar binary reading it is\ndangerous rather than merely limited: it would fetch only its single configured project, see every\nother project's bound tickets as having no corresponding remote issue, and create duplicate issues in\nthe wrong project. There is a shipped mechanism for exactly this — `.store-compat.json` with a\nfail-closed read (`src/rebar/_store/compat.py`) — but `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES` is still an empty frozenset\n(`compat.py:60`), so no capability has ever been declared through it.\n\n## Approach\n\nRegister `multi-project-bridge` in `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES`. That single addition is what makes a binary\nable to *recognise* the capability; a binary that predates it hits the \"required capability this\nbinary does not provide\" branch and raises `StoreIncompatibleError`, refusing writes rather than\ncorrupting the store (`docs/migrations.md:158-165`).\n\nThis is the expand half of the expand/contract rollout `docs/migrations.md:138-149` describes: teach\nbinaries to read and fail closed **before** anything writes the requirement. Registering the name here\nis inert on its own — nothing stamps it in this story, so shipping it changes no behaviour for any\nexisting store. The conditional stamp lands separately, which is why the two are ordered rather than\ncombined.\n\nReads deliberately stay available: the gate is on the write lock only\n(`docs/migrations.md:174-178`), so `list`/`show`/`search` keep working against a store an old binary\nmay not write, and `fsck` surfaces the condition as a structured `compat_error` without changing its\nexit code.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/compat.py`\n- tests under `tests/`\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard's pure-branch row: an in-process unit test against the real\nclassification function, since the mechanism is entirely a validation branch with no I/O of its own —\nplus one real-store test for the write-gate, because the gate fires inside lock acquisition and a\nunit test would not cross that component.\n\n- Happy path: a record declaring `multi-project-bridge` classifies as compatible on a binary that\n  registers it.\n- Contrast case: a record declaring an unregistered capability name still raises\n  `StoreIncompatibleError` — proving the registration widened the known set by exactly one entry and\n  did not disable the check.\n- Absent-record regression: a store with no `.store-compat.json` still passes through as implicit\n  legacy, so pre-feature stores are unaffected.\n- Write-gate path: a store whose record declares an unknown capability refuses a write through the\n  real lock acquisition, while `list`/`show` against the same store still succeed. The read half is\n  the contrast case that proves the gate is scoped to writes.\n- Corrupt-record path: a malformed record still raises rather than being treated as absent, which is\n  the bypass the gate is designed to prevent.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `multi-project-bridge` is in `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES` and a record declaring it classifies as\n      compatible; checked by a unit test over the classification function.\n- [ ] A record declaring an unregistered capability still raises `StoreIncompatibleError`; checked by\n      the paired negative case.\n- [ ] A store with no compat record still passes through as implicit legacy; checked by an\n      absent-record regression test.\n- [ ] A store declaring an unknown capability refuses writes while reads still succeed; checked by a\n      real-store test exercising the write lock and a read command against the same store.\n- [ ] A corrupt record raises rather than being treated as absent; checked by a malformed-record test.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/compat.py","reason":"register multi-project-bridge in KNOWN_CAPABILITIES"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_store_compat_multi_project.py","reason":"known vs unknown capability, absent record, write-gate scoping"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","574a-3152-5cef-430e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"178fb9b9-0981-4008-9fad-527d4d45274a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"67f9-4a07-9667-446a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Register the multi-project-bridge store-compat capability (expand half)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a9dfd20f-3575-4f2d-8fc6-c563039ac291","467500cc-c08e-43a3-8d0e-376454e601d5","f076d1e4-d223-4bf8-8f3a-ca9139c54e63","d3254257-d2f6-4659-9190-9c67645344c6","178fb9b9-0981-4008-9fad-527d4d45274a","80c8756e-5315-41ab-97e8-ec74af980184","d98cd0c7-b4cb-4330-af29-e22be9437654"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659615015395001,"uuid":"baf6dae3-9cce-4483-b34b-6db1a204e22f"}